  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-109447\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>Remember that slope is the amount the line rises vertically per unit that it runs horizontally.</p>\n<p>Since the graph increases (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"20\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2197\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">↗</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>) as we go from left to right, the line rises by a positive amount.</p>\n<p>Therefore, the slope of the line is positive.</p>\n</div>",
